  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Combine the stock powder and 1L (4 cups) water in a large saucepan and bring to the boil. Meanwhile, separate the pak choy leaves from the bunch, leaving them whole. Drain and rinse the corn.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/913689/photos/large/167176_1-2151d4963ce943f18e863a3fe21fa5ef.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook dumplings: Add the dumplings to the boiling stock and cook for 2 mins. Stir in the vegetable mix, pak choy and corn and cook for a further 2 mins or until the dumplings are cooked through and the veggies are tender. Stir in 2 tsp soy sauce, then remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/913690/photos/large/167176_2-73bdf714dd0891368cff034748497b0c.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the dumpling soup among bowls. Pick the coriander leaves and scatter over the top. Drizzle with the hoisin sauce and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/913691/photos/large/167176_3-f89aa71c2bb43f2448e5cad8572a4eef.jpeg"
    },
